  "projectUrl": "https://fsprojects.github.io/fantomas/",
  "published": "2026-09-12T08:51:50.173Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "### Changed\n\n- Updated the packages the command line tool is built against: `editorconfig` to `0.18.0`, `Serilog` to `4.4.0`, `Spectre.Console` to `0.57.2` and `System.IO.Abstractions` to `22.2.0`. Only one of these is visible in what Fantomas does: `editorconfig` `0.18.0` scopes its cache of the `.editorconfig` files it has read to the parser that reads them, where it used to share one statically. Fantomas keeps a single parser for the process, so a file is still read once and no more. `Fantomas.Core` asks for the same `FSharp.Core` it always did, so nothing referencing it has to move. [#3468](https://github.com/fsprojects/fantomas/pull/3468)",
